ilya2@rcn.com wrote:
> In Minetown, I acquired a pet djinni by rubbing a lamp. It followed me
> into two shops, where it behaved like any other pet -- picked up and
> dropped items, carried one or two out of the shop. Then I took this
> djinni up to DL 4 and into armor shop. All of a sudden the djinni
> attacks the shopkeeper (no, his name was not Itzhack!) and kills him.
> So, why in that shop and not in others? BTW, the slain shopkeeper had a
> wand of magic missiles, which I believe is on the weak side for the
> shopkeepers. Was that a factor?

Pets will attack based on their current level and hitpoints.
If the shopkeeper is one level higher than the pet, or any where below
that, and the pet currently has more than a quarter of its hitpoints,
it will attack.
Perhaps the djinn gained a level or two, or maybe the shopkeeper was
weaker.
It has nothing to do with the shopkeeper's inventory, by the way;
besides, most shopkeepers only have 1 wand (of striking).



